
# Striver's DSA Journey — Java

My daily journey of learning Data Structures and Algorithms
using Java, following Striver's Master DSA Patterns sheet.

## Goals
- Build strong problem-solving fundamentals.
- Learn and apply common DSA patterns.
- Analyze time and space complexity.
- Prepare for service-based and product-based company interviews.

## Progress

| Topic | Problems Solved |
|---|---:|
| Arrays | 0 |
| Hashing | 0 |
| Two Pointers | 0 |
| Binary Search | 0 |
| Linked Lists | 0 |
| Stacks and Queues | 0 |
| Trees and Graphs | 0 |
| Dynamic Programming | 0 |

## My Approach

For every problem, I aim to document:
- The problem statement and source.
- The approach and key observation.
- Time and space complexity.
- Edge cases and lessons learned.

